Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/aout-cris.c
Line: 248
Function: MY (swap_ext_reloc_in)
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: r_type is decoded from two bits (0..3). Values 0..2 are valid, but when r_type == 3 the code only logs an error and continues to set cache_ptr->howto = howto_table_ext + r_type. This indexes past the end of the howto_table_ext table (which holds only the 3 valid entries), causing an out-of-bounds read.

Source context:
